# SYNOPSIS

```usage
vx fsck file [name]
```

# DESCRIPTION

`vx fsck` mounts the Taisce volume on the partition <name> of the disk image <file> (the first Taisce partition, without a name) and checks it: every node read and checked against the checksum its parent keeps, and every invariant of its trees, free space, links and names.
It prints the transaction group the volume is at, its files and directories, and its blocks in use.
Mounting it frees what a crash left orphaned, as any mount does, so a volume a node was writing when it stopped is changed by being checked.

# EXAMPLES

```text
% vx fsck disk.img
fsck: disk.img taisce: clean at txg 3; 3 files and directories;
295 of 16123 blocks in use
```

# SEE ALSO

vx-disk(1), fs(4)

# DIAGNOSTICS

`no GUID partition table`, `no such partition`, or why the volume didn't mount or check, and it exits 1; 0 if it is clean.
